        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 24 at 3:31PM CDT by NWS Norman OK</headline>
        <description>At 330 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 4
miles northeast of May, moving northeast at 30 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Buffalo, May, and Selman.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
